<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; this.result <= i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i);</code>

However, since the method returns `-1` when there is no such bit, we need to adjust the assertion to account for this case. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> (\result == -1 || \forall int i; this.result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i));</code>

This ensures that if the result is not `-1`, then all bits between the result and the starting index are set to `true`. If the result is `-1`, it means there are no clear bits in the specified range, so the assertion holds trivially.
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; fromIndex >= i && i > \result; this.get(i);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 ==> \forall int i; fromIndex >= i && i > \result; this.get(i);</code>
